  <participating-org role="4" type="24">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main goal of Selasar Sunaryo Foundation (Yayasan Selasar Sunaryo/YSS) is to become a legal/
umbrella organization that supportsall program and activities at Selasar Sunaryo Art Space (SSAS), a
cultural centre located in Bandung, whose missions are:
1. To become a center for studies, research, exhibition and public art education of Indonesian art and
11
culture
2. To create a safe, open and free space for diversity of artistic expressions in Indonesia
3. To promote better understanding on the development of Indonesiancontemporary art and culture
through local and international collaboration
SSAS organizes exhibitions, discussions, residencies andworkshops related to other art disciplines such
as design, craft, performing arts, literature,architecture, and so on. All types ofactivities at SSAS&#x2014;
including children&apos;s programs, music concerts, theater performances, film screenings, literary readings,
workshop, lectures and various other activities&#x2014;are designed under the direction of the Curatorial
Advisory Boards consisting of academics, critics and art practitioners. SSAS&#x2019; flagship of event includes
Bandung New Emergence, a contemporary art exhibition of young artists (biannually, since 2006),
Selasar Kids Program, art and cultural program designed specially for kids (annually, since 2014),
Transit, a residency and exhibition program for Indonesian self-taught artists (biannually, since 2012)
and Mimbar Selasar, a cultural lecture program (annually, since 2017).
SSAS always emphasizes on educational contents in its each program. Its main facilities includes
Pustaka Selasar, which host a collection of hundreds of art and cultural books and digital archives.
Since its inception in 1998, SSAS has also been engaged in collaboration with various local and foreign
institutions, and curated hundreds of program that reached a wide scale of audiences ranging from
children, teenagers, students to art professionals/adults. SSAS&#x2019; Visitor attendances reaches (approx.)
50,000 per annum (local and international, as per 2019). Since 2017, public engagement has intensified
with the specially designed social media content, which attracts more youth audiences attending
activities at SSAS.
SSAS important accomplishment includes networking and cooperation to support the promotion of
Indonesian artists at international levels.</narrative>
